# aside-rule battery: tests aside_rule's plain-lookup behavior directly -- one worthy case (a genuinely notable fact should trigger one extra sentence), one flat case (nothing should trigger). Real check is the A/B run against FELLA_PROMPT_DROP=aside_rule, not this gold alone. Gold computed by bench/aside-rule/gen.py from the copied file, not hand-typed.
{"id": "ar-worthy-rent", "question": "What was my total spending on rent in 2024?", "files": ["spend.csv"], "gold": {"contains": ["15013.23", "59%|dominant|largest|most of|majority"]}, "tier": "aside-worthy", "domain": "spending", "multifile": false, "n_files": 1, "formats": ["csv"]}
{"id": "ar-flat-utilities", "question": "What was my total spending on utilities in 2024?", "files": ["spend.csv"], "gold": {"figures": [1776.64]}, "tier": "aside-flat", "domain": "spending", "multifile": false, "n_files": 1, "formats": ["csv"]}
